comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T08:59:18.441Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status searches for CodeQL improper code sanitization, generated extension artifact path, and security code injection found the general quality epic pm-92if and prior CodeQL workflow-hardening work, but no item tracking this PR-specific scanner finding. Created as a child of the active review exemplar pm-mav1ak and implementation of pm-92if."
  "2026-08-17T09:00:48.160Z","harness:codex","TDD and remediation evidence: CodeQL alert #36 identified a harness-controlled path embedded into generated JavaScript. The integration fixture now passes that path as runtime environment data, validates its presence inside the disposable extension, and retains the same file-artifact assertion. Focused integration coverage passes 8/8, the linked PM test passes, file-level ESLint passes, and git diff validation is clean. Hosted CodeQL remains the mandatory exact-head negative control."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T09:00:48.851Z","harness:codex","Even test-only generated modules should preserve the data/code boundary: pass variable fixture coordinates at runtime instead of serializing them into source, so scanners can distinguish trusted code from data without suppressions."
